Java notes:

* public    : same
* private   : same
* protected : same
* final     : same + const/constexpr
* virtual   : all non-static methods are virtual by default (unless final or private)

* abstract  : same as pure-virtual functions
    void on_update() = 0;
    - Dog extends Animal (single inheritance)

* interface : same as virtual class
    only pure-virtual functions and constants
    Multiple inheritance: implements keyword
    default method: interface fallback for a virtual function

Packages:
    package com.example.game    lives inside    com/example/game/
    classes in the same package (folder) can see private from other classes
